# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of platform or
# local core.autocrlf settings. Windows installs of Git commonly ship with
# core.autocrlf=true, which silently rewrites every checked-out text file to
# CRLF; tools that snapshot raw working-copy bytes without applying Git's
# clean/smudge filters (e.g. `jj`) then see every such file as "modified"
# even with zero real edits. Forcing eol=lf here keeps the working tree and
# the repository byte-for-byte consistent.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Preserve native line endings for assets where CRLF is meaningful/expected.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
